lock it.\n- **Test:** I added a case to `response_writer_test.go` that sends a 101 header and then hijacks; it must succeed. The existing case that hijacks after a body write still gets `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n- **Results:** `go test ./...` passes and `gofmt` reports nothing.\n\nI didn't test this against a real WebSocket library. The changes are uncommitted and HEAD is detached; tell me if you want me to commit with your message.","ttft_ms":2607,"type":"result","duration_ms":24987,"uuid":"43039756-1d2e-4433-9256-4fe6544fc70f","ttft_stream_ms":1055,"time_to_request_ms":136,"first_content_frame_ms":1055,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
